# .prettierignore — paths Prettier must not rewrite.
#
# Owns the formatter's exclusion list. Two categories:
#   1. Generated or vendored output that would be reformatted pointlessly on every run.
#   2. Files whose exact byte content is meaningful and must not be reflowed.

# Generated / installed
node_modules
.next
out
build
dist
coverage
# Playwright's generated output. Prettier currently also honours `.gitignore`, which
# already lists these, so this is belt-and-braces rather than a live fix — but the
# formatter's exclusions should not depend on a default that a future Prettier major
# could change. ESLint needs the same three paths spelled out in `eslint.config.mjs`,
# where they are NOT redundant: ESLint does not read `.gitignore` at all.
playwright-report
test-results
.playwright
next-env.d.ts
package-lock.json
# Planning and process documents owned by the human and by other agents. Prettier's
# markdown reflow would produce enormous, meaningless diffs in these.
PLANNING.md
CLAUDE.md
QA/
.claude/

# Binary/asset directories
public/images
